.TH elfshaker-pack 1  "pack " 
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-pack \- Packs the given snapshots into a pack file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker pack\fR [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-compression\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\fR] [\fB\-\-snapshots\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-snapshots0\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIname\fR> [\fIindexes\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Packs the given snapshots into a pack file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR [default: 0]
Use the specified number of worker threads for compression. The number of threads used is proportional to the memory needed for compression.
.TP
\fB\-\-compression\-level\fR [default: 10]
The ZStandard compression level to use (up to 22). Negative values enable fast compression.
.TP
\fB\-\-frames\fR [default: 0]
The number of frames to emit in the pack file. A lower number of frames limits the number of decompression processes that can run concurrently. A higher number of frames can result in poorer compression. Specify 0 to auto\-detect the appropriate number of frames to emit.
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshots\-from\fR \fI<file>\fR
Reads the list of snapshots to include in the pack from the specified file. \*(Aq\-\*(Aq is taken to mean stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshots0\-from\fR \fI<file>\fR
Reads the NUL\-separated (ASCII \\0) list of snapshots to include in the pack from the specified file. \*(Aq\-\*(Aq is taken to mean stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enables verbose description of the execution process.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Set the path to the elfshaker repository.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIname\fR>
Specifies the name of the pack to create.
.TP
[\fIindexes\fR]
Specify the indexes of packs to include.
